From: =?UTF-8?q?Enrico=20B=C3=BChler?= <enrico.buehler@unom.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:32:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(console): add the Tizen platform
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The browser client packaged as a Samsung TV app fronts the shell as
Platform::Web, which cannot quit — and Samsung requires Back at an app's
root to exit — and which draws the keyboard glyph legend for a page
held by a remote. Platform::Tizen answers the row tables exactly as Web
does, takes the TV glyph legend, can quit, and offers the codec row
without AV1 and PyroWave, which the set does not decode.

The bridge's CreateOptions gains a `tizen` flag for the browser host to
name the platform; the native hosts name theirs in code.
